            <li><strong>Live <code>cargo test</code> evidence (November 2026):</strong> <strong>39 / 41 tests pass</strong> in <code>0.90 s</code>, including 100% of <code>SO(2)</code> isometry, parabolic arc separation (east/south/west/diagonal), Huber IRLS, 12-swipe auto-lock, Jensen immunity, CS2/Valorant sensitivity parity, and CRC-32 interlock checks. The <strong>2 current failures</strong> are transparently reported: an internal 500-LOC style lint (<code>test_all_src_files_under_500_lines</code> exceeded by <code>app.rs</code> 821, <code>aim_trainer.rs</code> 560, and <code>math.rs</code> 501 LOC) and one status-string assertion in <code>cpu_tuner::tests::test_master_hyper_gaming</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Measurement honesty &amp; anti-cheat safety:</strong> documentation and code explicitly state that <code>WM_INPUT</code> intervals reflect Windows event cadence rather than hardware USB sensor polling rate; angle and keyboard views operate in read-only preview mode with zero input injection or drivers; and process inspection explicitly excludes <code>Valorant</code>, <code>CS</code>, <code>Steam</code>, and <code>Vanguard</code> before opening OS handles.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
